# Naming conventions

Use these names in new folders and C++ we add. Do not silently rename existing lowercase folders (`src/core`, `src/maps`, …) unless the team asks.

## Folders — first letter uppercase (PascalCase)

Each path segment starts with an uppercase letter. Further words are uppercase too.

- ✅ `Player/`, `SpikeFloor/`, `Maps/House/`
- ❌ `player/`, `spike_floor/`, `maps/house/`

Leave these as-is: CMake output `build/`, tool dirs (`.cursor`, `.git`), and the existing `src/` tree until it is renamed on purpose.

## Variables — camelCase

Start lowercase. Every later word starts uppercase.

- ✅ `playerMovement`, `heartPosition`, `trapCount`
- ❌ `PlayerMovement`, `player_movement`, `HeartPosition`

Match `inline constexpr` constants in `game_constants.hpp`: `hh::MAX_PLAYERS`, `hh::BUILD_TIME_SEC` (ALL_CAPS). Do not camelCase those. Do not `#define` them.

## Functions — PascalCase

Start uppercase. Every later word starts uppercase.

- ✅ `UpdatePlayer()`, `PlaceTrap()`, `CheckHeartTouch()`
- ❌ `updatePlayer()`, `place_trap()`, `check_heart_touch()`

Raylib APIs we call (`InitWindow`, `BeginDrawing`) already match this. Do not wrap them in snake_case helpers just to rename them.

## Files

- Headers we own use `.hpp` (`spike_floor.hpp`, `locked_door.hpp`, `game_constants.hpp`).
- Implementation files stay `.cpp`.
- Do not add new `.h` files for our code. Leave third-party headers as they ship (`raylib.h`).
